  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Signal Box Panel",
    "overview": "DriftGuard is drawn as the illuminated track diagram in a railway signal box. Each agent task is a train on a line, tools are block sections, and the tool that holds the line is the section lit red. Drift is distance from a baseline, drawn as a gauge with the floor engraved on it. The surface is a dark green-black enamel panel with ivory engraved lettering and hairline rules, never pure black and never a grid of equal KPI cards.\n\nColour is quarantined. A healthy view is ink on enamel; the lamp colours (red, amber, green) appear only where state deviates, and always as a lit lamp with an icon and a word. Density is that of an operator's desk: compact, ruled, legible at a glance, with poster-scale condensed figures for the numbers that matter.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Enamel panel surfaces separated by 1px hairline rules, not by shadow or fill contrast.",
      "Ivory \"route\" colour carries selection, the primary action, focus and the lit track.",
      "Lamps, never decorative colour, carry state; state is never colour alone (icon, word, hatch).",
      "Engraved plate labels (condensed, uppercase, open tracking) name every instrument.",
      "Instruments sit in one ruled strip, not in separate cards."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Quarantine Rule",
        "body": "Lamp red, amber and green mean a state. They never decorate, and a healthy screen has none of them lit.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never-Colour-Alone Rule",
        "body": "Every lamp state is also written in words with an icon, and out-of-limit spans are hatched.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraved Label Rule",
        "body": "Names of instruments and field groups are plate labels: condensed, uppercase, 0.08em tracking, Muted. Nothing else is set that way.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number that changes is set with tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Plate Rule",
        "body": "Resting panels carry no shadow. If it is not floating, it is ruled, not lifted.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep healthy views as Ink and Route on Enamel, and let lamp colour appear only where state deviates.",
      "**Do** pair every lamp or red/amber/green tone with an icon and a word.",
      "**Do** separate surfaces with 1px Hairline rules and tonal steps (canvas, panel, raised).",
      "**Do** set instrument names as plate labels and large readings as condensed tabular figures.",
      "**Do** keep a visible 2px Route focus outline and honour `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "**Do** set identifiers, tool names and error strings in JetBrains Mono."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** build a grid of equal KPI cards over a dark console; group readings in a ruled instrument strip.",
      "**Don't** use pure black, or lamp colours as decoration or chart fill for non-state data.",
      "**Don't** convey state by colour alone.",
      "**Don't** add resting shadows to panels, or corners larger than 8px.",
      "**Don't** introduce another accent beside Route Ivory for actions."
    ]
  }
}